[ ] Project recurring occurrences into the action surfaces =occurrence-surface $Client-surface follow-on to VTODO sync: the action list becomes a windowed union of materialized actions + projected occurrences (render(master+deviations, window)). Occurrences have no .actions line. Seam: operations uniform, text-editing not. See README 'Client-surface projection (2026-07-24)'.$ !2 #019f962c-ba5a-7732-ad24-df6fceadea53
    >[ ] Ingest a foreign roll-forward as occurrence completion $Invariant, and a BUILD task (needs the deviation write-model to exist first). A camp-B client (Apple Reminders etc.) completes a recurring VTODO by advancing the master DTSTART with no override. Import must recognize 'master advanced one period, no new override' as completion of the prior occurrence and record that deviation, not reinterpret it as a series reschedule. No RECURRENCE-ID/master-advance detection exists today — greenfield, not verify-only.$ !1 #019f962c-eb46-77b3-931e-1e43920e7daa
    >[ ] Render the windowed union of actions and projected occurrences in the views =occurrence-view $Union LANDED (2026-07-25): From<Workspace> for DomainModel renders + unions occurrences at the single lowering; CLI read path surfaces them (window from expansion_total_instances); occurrences addressable by their occurrence UUIDv5; deterministic under a fixed Projection. REMAINING: consolidate the TWO assembly sites — the union is currently assembled both in From<Workspace> and in the CLI collect_all_actions (both via the one render_occurrences primitive, so no logic dup, but two sites). collect_all_actions uses load_workspace (MarkdownCharter, for file-path/-f needs) rather than the projected model; fold these into one path so no consumer re-assembles. Also depends on the frame fix for deviated occurrences to render correctly.$ !2 #019f962c-eb51-72a3-9ab9-73b93dad5959
    >[ ] Route occurrence operations to deviations, not line edits =occurrence-ops $complete/skip LANDED (2026-07-25): cancel->EXDATE, complete->completed RECURRENCE-ID override, via core write_occurrence_deviation (ics.rs) + apply_occurrence_op (plans.rs). CLI complete/cancel fall through to occurrence handling only when the query is not a materialized line (materialized wins). Handle = plan_id + external_occurrence_key stamped on each rendered occurrence. e2e-proven via the real binary. REMAINING: reschedule (needs datetime args, likely update <occurrence> --scheduled-at).$ !2 <occurrence-view #019f962d-1f07-7091-a4af-9868afc2a1aa
    >[ ] Surface occurrences in nvim as virtual lines and code-actions $Keep the buffer honest: occurrences render as virtual lines/extmarks, never editable buffer text with nowhere to save back. Expose complete/reschedule/skip as LSP code-actions that invoke the occurrence-ops write path. org-agenda two-surface model: raw-file editing unchanged for materialized actions.$ !3 <occurrence-ops #019f962d-1f15-7c23-82d5-e1c8f2a652e0
    >[ ] Retire expand materialization and the upcoming file $Demolition the projection model implies. Remove expand_plans_into_actions file-writing, <charter>.upcoming.actions, and expansion_primary_instances. Occurrences are projected on the fly at load, never filed; the window collapses to a single per-plan count (expansion_total_instances). A materialized occurrence line was a second master that drifts from its RRULE; projection dissolves the drift. See README design notes 2026-07-24 cont.$ !1 #019f9794-de24-7ca3-8807-9c88f81f5a96
    >[ ] Strip calendar-only sidecar fields $Enabled by retiring materialization. Remove ActionMeta.external_schedule_id (no materialized generated lines remain to re-link; a projected occurrence carries plan linkage inherently in memory) and PlanMeta.last_expanded (nothing expands). Leave charter.id/charter.created/ActionMeta.created — generic provenance orthogonal to calendar sync, whose own fate is a separate workspace charter's call.$ !2 #019f9794-de34-7bc0-937a-73e4df2fb3b1
    >[x] Seal the projection to sync leak $Sync reconciles owned artifacts only; a projected occurrence has no standalone resource to reconcile and no line for apply_sync to locate. sync_calendar now loads a window-0 model (Projection::without_occurrences / ctx.load_model_materialized) so occurrences are structurally absent from plan_sync, not filtered by a fragile flag. Regression-locked in workspace_store.rs. Relates to the two-assembly-sites debt in =occurrence-view.$ #019f9bdf-bad8-7940-a77e-98be6bf8b04e
